# Chat Microservice — React Frontend Implementation Guide

## Overview

This guide explains how to integrate the **recruitable-chat-service** (port 8082) into your React frontend. The chat service provides REST APIs for CRUD operations and WebSocket (STOMP) for real-time messaging.

---

## 1. Install Dependencies

```bash
npm install @stomp/stompjs sockjs-client
npm install -D @types/sockjs-client  # if using TypeScript
```

---

## 2. API Configuration

```typescript
// src/config/chat.ts
export const CHAT_API_BASE = 'http://localhost:8082/api/v1/chat';
export const CHAT_WS_URL = 'http://localhost:8082/ws';
```

All REST requests must include the JWT access token from the main backend auth:

```typescript
// src/services/chatApi.ts
import axios from 'axios';
import { CHAT_API_BASE } from '../config/chat';

const chatApi = axios.create({
  baseURL: CHAT_API_BASE,
});

chatApi.interceptors.request.use((config) => {
  const token = localStorage.getItem('access_token'); // or from your auth store
  if (token) {
    config.headers.Authorization = `Bearer ${token}`;
  }
  return config;
});

export default chatApi;
```

---

## 3. REST API Integration

### 3.1 Create a Chat Room

```typescript
// PRIVATE room (1-on-1 DM)
const createPrivateRoom = async (otherUserId: string) => {
  const response = await chatApi.post('/rooms', {
    type: 'PRIVATE',
    member_user_ids: [otherUserId],
  });
  return response.data; // ChatRoomResponse
};

// GROUP room (channel)
const createGroupRoom = async (name: string, memberIds: string[]) => {
  const response = await chatApi.post('/rooms', {
    type: 'GROUP',
    name,
    description: 'Optional description',
    member_user_ids: memberIds,
  });
  return response.data;
};
```

### 3.2 List Rooms

```typescript
const getRooms = async () => {
  const response = await chatApi.get('/rooms');
  return response.data; // ChatRoomResponse[]
};
```

**Response shape** (snake_case due to Jackson config):

```json
[
  {
    "id": "uuid",
    "organization_id": "uuid",
    "type": "GROUP",
    "name": "Engineering Team",
    "description": "...",
    "avatar_url": null,
    "created_at": "2026-04-05T10:00:00Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-04-05T12:30:00Z",
    "members": [
      {
        "user_id": "uuid",
        "role": "OWNER",
        "joined_at": "2026-04-05T10:00:00Z",
        "last_read_at": "2026-04-05T12:28:00Z"
      }
    ],
    "unread_count": 3,
    "last_message": {
      "id": "uuid",
      "room_id": "uuid",
      "sender_id": "uuid",
      "type": "TEXT",
      "body": "Hello everyone!",
      "created_at": "2026-04-05T12:30:00Z"
    }
  }
]
```

### 3.3 Get Message History

```typescript
const getMessages = async (roomId: string, page = 0, size = 50) => {
  const response = await chatApi.get(`/rooms/${roomId}/messages`, {
    params: { page, size },
  });
  return response.data; // PageResponse<ChatMessageResponse>
};
```

**Response:**

```json
{
  "content": [
    {
      "id": "uuid",
      "room_id": "uuid",
      "sender_id": "uuid",
      "sender_name": null,
      "type": "TEXT",
      "body": "Hello!",
      "parent_message_id": null,
      "file_url": null,
      "file_name": null,
      "file_size": null,
      "file_content_type": null,
      "edited": false,
      "deleted": false,
      "created_at": "2026-04-05T12:30:00Z",
      "edited_at": null
    }
  ],
  "page": 0,
  "size": 50,
  "total_elements": 120,
  "total_pages": 3,
  "first": true,
  "last": false
}
```

### 3.4 Send Message via REST

```typescript
const sendMessage = async (roomId: string, body: string) => {
  const response = await chatApi.post(`/rooms/${roomId}/messages`, {
    body,
    type: 'TEXT',
  });
  return response.data;
};
```

### 3.5 Edit / Delete Message

```typescript
const editMessage = async (messageId: string, body: string) => {
  const response = await chatApi.put(`/messages/${messageId}`, { body });
  return response.data;
};

const deleteMessage = async (messageId: string) => {
  await chatApi.delete(`/messages/${messageId}`);
};
```

### 3.6 Mark Room as Read

```typescript
const markAsRead = async (roomId: string) => {
  await chatApi.post(`/rooms/${roomId}/read`);
};
```

### 3.7 Upload File

```typescript
const uploadFile = async (file: File) => {
  const formData = new FormData();
  formData.append('file', file);
  const response = await chatApi.post('/files/upload', formData, {
    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'multipart/form-data' },
  });
  return response.data; // { file_url, file_name, file_size, content_type }
};
```

### 3.8 Get Online Users

```typescript
const getOnlineUsers = async () => {
  const response = await chatApi.get('/users/online');
  return response.data; // string[] (user IDs)
};
```

---

## 4. WebSocket (STOMP) Integration

### 4.1 STOMP Client Setup

```typescript
// src/services/chatWebSocket.ts
import { Client, IMessage, StompSubscription } from '@stomp/stompjs';
import SockJS from 'sockjs-client';
import { CHAT_WS_URL } from '../config/chat';

let stompClient: Client | null = null;

export const connectChat = (
  token: string,
  orgId: string,
  onConnect: () => void,
  onDisconnect: () => void
) => {
  stompClient = new Client({
    // Use SockJS as the transport
    webSocketFactory: () => new SockJS(CHAT_WS_URL),

    connectHeaders: {
      Authorization: `Bearer ${token}`,
    },

    // Reconnect every 5 seconds if disconnected
    reconnectDelay: 5000,

    onConnect: () => {
      console.log('Chat WebSocket connected');
      onConnect();
    },

    onDisconnect: () => {
      console.log('Chat WebSocket disconnected');
      onDisconnect();
    },

    onStompError: (frame) => {
      console.error('STOMP error:', frame.headers['message']);
    },
  });

  stompClient.activate();
  return stompClient;
};

export const disconnectChat = () => {
  if (stompClient) {
    stompClient.deactivate();
    stompClient = null;
  }
};

export const getStompClient = () => stompClient;
```

### 4.2 Subscribe to Room Messages

```typescript
export const subscribeToRoom = (
  orgId: string,
  roomId: string,
  onMessage: (message: ChatMessageResponse) => void
): StompSubscription | null => {
  if (!stompClient || !stompClient.connected) return null;

  return stompClient.subscribe(
    `/topic/org.${orgId}.room.${roomId}`,
    (msg: IMessage) => {
      const message = JSON.parse(msg.body);
      onMessage(message);
    }
  );
};
```

### 4.3 Subscribe to Typing Indicators

```typescript
export const subscribeToTyping = (
  orgId: string,
  roomId: string,
  onTyping: (event: TypingEvent) => void
): StompSubscription | null => {
  if (!stompClient || !stompClient.connected) return null;

  return stompClient.subscribe(
    `/topic/org.${orgId}.room.${roomId}.typing`,
    (msg: IMessage) => {
      onTyping(JSON.parse(msg.body));
    }
  );
};
```

### 4.4 Subscribe to Presence (Online/Offline)

```typescript
export const subscribeToPresence = (
  orgId: string,
  onEvent: (event: WebSocketEventDto) => void
): StompSubscription | null => {
  if (!stompClient || !stompClient.connected) return null;

  return stompClient.subscribe(
    `/topic/org.${orgId}.presence`,
    (msg: IMessage) => {
      onEvent(JSON.parse(msg.body));
    }
  );
};
```

### 4.5 Subscribe to Room Changes (Created, Member Added/Removed)

```typescript
export const subscribeToRoomChanges = (
  orgId: string,
  onEvent: (event: WebSocketEventDto) => void
): StompSubscription | null => {
  if (!stompClient || !stompClient.connected) return null;

  // Events: ROOM_CREATED, MEMBER_ADDED, MEMBER_REMOVED
  return stompClient.subscribe(
    `/topic/org.${orgId}.rooms`,
    (msg: IMessage) => {
      onEvent(JSON.parse(msg.body));
    }
  );
};
```

### 4.6 Subscribe to Room Membership Changes

```typescript
export const subscribeToRoomMembers = (
  orgId: string,
  roomId: string,
  onEvent: (event: WebSocketEventDto) => void
): StompSubscription | null => {
  if (!stompClient || !stompClient.connected) return null;

  return stompClient.subscribe(
    `/topic/org.${orgId}.room.${roomId}.members`,
    (msg: IMessage) => {
      onEvent(JSON.parse(msg.body));
    }
  );
};
```

### 4.7 Send a Message via WebSocket

```typescript
export const sendMessageWs = (roomId: string, body: string, type = 'TEXT') => {
  if (!stompClient || !stompClient.connected) return;

  stompClient.publish({
    destination: '/app/chat.send',
    body: JSON.stringify({
      room_id: roomId,
      body,
      type,
    }),
  });
};
```

### 4.8 Send Typing Indicator

```typescript
export const sendTypingIndicator = (roomId: string, typing: boolean) => {
  if (!stompClient || !stompClient.connected) return;

  stompClient.publish({
    destination: '/app/chat.typing',
    body: JSON.stringify({
      room_id: roomId,
      typing,
    }),
  });
};
```

### 4.9 Send Read Receipt via WebSocket

```typescript
export const sendReadReceipt = (roomId: string) => {
  if (!stompClient || !stompClient.connected) return;

  stompClient.publish({
    destination: '/app/chat.read',
    body: JSON.stringify({
      room_id: roomId,
    }),
  });
};
```

---

## 5. React Hook Example

```typescript
// src/hooks/useChat.ts
import { useEffect, useRef, useState, useCallback } from 'react';
import { useAuth } from './useAuth'; // your existing auth hook
import {
  connectChat,
  disconnectChat,
  subscribeToRoom,
  subscribeToTyping,
  subscribeToPresence,
  sendMessageWs,
  sendTypingIndicator,
} from '../services/chatWebSocket';
import chatApi from '../services/chatApi';

interface ChatMessage {
  id: string;
  room_id: string;
  sender_id: string;
  type: string;
  body: string;
  created_at: string;
  edited: boolean;
  deleted: boolean;
}

export const useChat = (roomId: string | null) => {
  const { token, user } = useAuth();
  const [messages, setMessages] = useState<ChatMessage[]>([]);
  const [typingUsers, setTypingUsers] = useState<Set<string>>(new Set());
  const [connected, setConnected] = useState(false);
  const subsRef = useRef<any[]>([]);

  // Connect WebSocket
  useEffect(() => {
    if (!token || !user?.organization_id) return;

    connectChat(
      token,
      user.organization_id,
      () => setConnected(true),
      () => setConnected(false)
    );

    return () => {
      disconnectChat();
    };
  }, [token, user?.organization_id]);

  // Subscribe to room
  useEffect(() => {
    if (!connected || !roomId || !user?.organization_id) return;

    // Load history
    chatApi
      .get(`/rooms/${roomId}/messages`, { params: { page: 0, size: 50 } })
      .then((res) => {
        setMessages(res.data.content.reverse()); // oldest first
      });

    // Subscribe to new messages
    const msgSub = subscribeToRoom(user.organization_id, roomId, (msg) => {
      setMessages((prev) => [...prev, msg]);
    });

    // Subscribe to typing
    const typingSub = subscribeToTyping(user.organization_id, roomId, (event) => {
      setTypingUsers((prev) => {
        const next = new Set(prev);
        if (event.typing) {
          next.add(event.user_id);
        } else {
          next.delete(event.user_id);
        }
        return next;
      });
    });

    subsRef.current = [msgSub, typingSub].filter(Boolean);

    return () => {
      subsRef.current.forEach((sub) => sub?.unsubscribe());
      subsRef.current = [];
    };
  }, [connected, roomId, user?.organization_id]);

  const sendMessage = useCallback(
    (body: string) => {
      if (roomId) sendMessageWs(roomId, body);
    },
    [roomId]
  );

  const sendTyping = useCallback(
    (typing: boolean) => {
      if (roomId) sendTypingIndicator(roomId, typing);
    },
    [roomId]
  );

  return { messages, typingUsers, connected, sendMessage, sendTyping };
};
```

---

## 6. File Upload Flow

1. User selects a file in the UI
2. Upload via REST: `POST /api/v1/chat/files/upload`
3. Get back `{ file_url, file_name, file_size, content_type }`
4. Send a FILE message with the URL:

```typescript
const handleFileUpload = async (file: File, roomId: string) => {
  // Step 1: Upload to S3
  const uploadResult = await uploadFile(file);

  // Step 2: Send as FILE message via WebSocket
  stompClient?.publish({
    destination: '/app/chat.send',
    body: JSON.stringify({
      room_id: roomId,
      type: 'FILE',
      body: uploadResult.file_name,
      file_url: uploadResult.file_url,
      file_name: uploadResult.file_name,
      file_size: uploadResult.file_size,
      file_content_type: uploadResult.content_type,
    }),
  });
};
```

---

## 7. TypeScript Interfaces

```typescript
// src/types/chat.ts

export interface ChatRoomResponse {
  id: string;
  organization_id: string;
  type: 'PRIVATE' | 'GROUP';
  name: string | null;
  description: string | null;
  avatar_url: string | null;
  created_at: string;
  updated_at: string;
  members: RoomMemberResponse[];
  unread_count: number;
  last_message: ChatMessageResponse | null;
}

export interface RoomMemberResponse {
  user_id: string;
  role: 'OWNER' | 'ADMIN' | 'MEMBER';
  joined_at: string;
  last_read_at: string | null;
}

export interface ChatMessageResponse {
  id: string;
  room_id: string;
  sender_id: string;
  sender_name: string | null;
  type: 'TEXT' | 'FILE' | 'SYSTEM';
  body: string | null;
  parent_message_id: string | null;
  file_url: string | null;
  file_name: string | null;
  file_size: number | null;
  file_content_type: string | null;
  edited: boolean;
  deleted: boolean;
  created_at: string;
  edited_at: string | null;
}

export interface TypingEvent {
  room_id: string;
  user_id: string;
  user_name: string | null;
  typing: boolean;
}

export interface WebSocketEventDto {
  event: string;
  user_id: string;
  timestamp: number;
}

export interface CreateRoomRequest {
  type: 'PRIVATE' | 'GROUP';
  name?: string;
  description?: string;
  member_user_ids: string[];
}

export interface SendMessageRequest {
  room_id: string;
  body?: string;
  type?: 'TEXT' | 'FILE';
  parent_message_id?: string;
  file_url?: string;
  file_name?: string;
  file_size?: number;
  file_content_type?: string;
}

export interface FileUploadResponse {
  file_url: string;
  file_name: string;
  file_size: number;
  content_type: string;
}

export interface PageResponse<T> {
  content: T[];
  page: number;
  size: number;
  total_elements: number;
  total_pages: number;
  first: boolean;
  last: boolean;
}
```

---

## 8. Component Architecture (Recommended)

```
src/features/chat/
├── ChatLayout.tsx          # Sidebar + message area layout
├── ChatSidebar.tsx         # Room list with search
├── RoomListItem.tsx        # Individual room row (name, last msg, unread badge)
├── MessageArea.tsx         # Message list + input for active room
├── MessageBubble.tsx       # Individual message (with edit/delete menu)
├── MessageInput.tsx        # Text input + file upload + typing indicator
├── TypingIndicator.tsx     # "User is typing..." display
├── OnlineStatus.tsx        # Green/gray dot for user presence
├── CreateRoomModal.tsx     # Modal to create GROUP room / start DM
├── RoomHeader.tsx          # Room name, members, actions
└── FilePreview.tsx         # Inline file/image preview in messages
```

---

## 9. Important Notes

1. **JWT Shared Secret**: The chat service uses the **same JWT secret** as the main backend. Users authenticate once via `recruitable-api-backend` and use the same token for chat.

2. **No User Table**: The chat service has NO user table. Sender identity comes from the JWT. If you need display names, either:
   - Pass `sender_name` in the `SendMessageRequest` payload
   - Fetch user details from the main backend and cache them in the frontend

3. **Org Isolation**: All WebSocket topic subscriptions are namespaced by `orgId`. The interceptor prevents subscribing to another org's channels.

4. **CORS**: The chat service allows all origins (`*`) for WebSocket. For REST, it also allows all origins. Tighten this in production.

5. **Swagger UI**: Available at `http://localhost:8082/swagger-ui/index.html`

# Chat Microservice — React Frontend Implementation Guide

## Overview

This guide explains how to integrate the **recruitable-chat-service** (port 8082) into your React frontend. The chat service provides REST APIs for CRUD operations and WebSocket (STOMP) for real-time messaging.

---

## 1. Install Dependencies

```bash
npm install @stomp/stompjs sockjs-client
npm install -D @types/sockjs-client  # if using TypeScript
```

---

## 2. API Configuration

```typescript
// src/config/chat.ts
export const CHAT_API_BASE = 'http://localhost:8082/api/v1/chat';
export const CHAT_WS_URL = 'http://localhost:8082/ws';
```

All REST requests must include the JWT access token from the main backend auth:

```typescript
// src/services/chatApi.ts
import axios from 'axios';
import { CHAT_API_BASE } from '../config/chat';

const chatApi = axios.create({
  baseURL: CHAT_API_BASE,
});

chatApi.interceptors.request.use((config) => {
  const token = localStorage.getItem('access_token'); // or from your auth store
  if (token) {
    config.headers.Authorization = `Bearer ${token}`;
  }
  return config;
});

export default chatApi;
```

